{"kind":"assert","text":"BO1-W1 ruling on 362bfe64 (plan d827e5b2). Approved: the separate dap-commons Worker, the commons cohort, the keys-only founding under SCOPE_INDEX_MODE=enforce with no open creation, the identity pair (REGISTER_SCOPE equal to ARTIFACTS_CONFIG.registerScope), removing DEMO_START_CONFIG, and the rollback with no automatic destructive cleanup. Custody: I run the plan and the provisioning from a private home under ~/.config/artroom/. Hugh holds the founder key and his own marks.\n\nOne blocker before any hosted action. The plan expires in 14 minutes, and the planned scope must be in the checked-in config before the deploy. A reviewed config commit cannot land in 14 minutes. Resolve the order and show it in the note:\n(a) whether the planned scope ID depends on the deadline, or only on the key and the intent; and\n(b) a sequence that fits. Either `--planned` can resubmit after expiry with the same scope ID, or the config commit is a two-value change whose review checks only those values against the retained plan. If it is the second, name the checks that change covers (gate stages that read wrangler.commons.jsonc) so I can rule on a focused run instead of a full gate.\n\nAdd to the note:\n1. A DO guard, because internal fanout is unmeasured. I read the dap-commons DO rate in 5-minute windows during W1. If any window exceeds 500 requests, stop W1 traffic and reconcile. After W1, read one idle hour. The expected idle rate is near zero, and above 100 per hour blocks further use.\n2. Hugh's time as one total, about 40 to 60 minutes, and the steps that need him in one block. I ask him for a time before provisioning.\nThen return the note for review. Notes-only gate and checker review as usual. I land it before provisioning.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}